{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation (read-only, 2026-11-12 ~05:55 PST)\nThe spend-cap Lambda (`/aws/lambda/bedrock-spend-cap` log, ticks from 13:41Z onward) reported the metered (ceiling-priced CloudWatch token) estimate at about 3 times the Cost Explorer figure for the same UTC day, with `effective_source=metered`. The metered arm crossed the daily threshold and attached `BedrockDailySpendCapDeny` (about 05:40 PST), denying `bedrock:InvokeModel` to every capped role, including rebar-gerrit-instance-role, until the 00:00 UTC release.\n\ninfra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/README.md documents the metered arm as an intentional upper bound, running at about 1.1 to 1.9 times settled billing. A ratio of about 3 is outside that band. Dollar figures are deliberately omitted (public tracker); they are in the Lambda log lines and Cost Explorer for 2026-11-12.\n\n## Root cause (measured; see comment)\nMost of the 3x was same-day Cost Explorer lag (re-read later, the 11-12 ratio is 1.94). The settled 2026-11-11 ratio is 2.04: the ceilings are tied to the 4.x price list, and for Opus 5.5 the cache-read ceiling is about 3.1x the billed rate (other directions about 1.56x), with cache reads about 90% of tokens. The ceilings still match their written definition; the documented band is stale.\n\n## Approach (decided 2026-11-12: README-only)\nUpdate `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/README.md`, ratios only:\n- Replace the 1.1-1.9x band with the measured band for the 5.5 generation (about 1.8x to 2.1x), stating that cache reads dominate: for Opus 5.5 the cache-read ceiling is about 3.1x the billed rate, the other directions about 1.56x.\n- Explain that a same-day Cost Explorer comparison overstates the ratio because Cost Explorer lags intra-day (the \"about 3x\" sighting), so the comparison must use settled days.\nNo change to the handler, threshold, attachment, or Terraform. A per-model exact-match rate table remains a possible future story (not filed): it is a new mechanism, out of scope for a bug fix.\n\n## Testing\nNew `tests/infra/test_bedrock_cap_readme_band.py`, ratios only (no prices): it encodes the Opus 5.5 ceiling-over-billed factors (1.5625 for input, output and cache write; 3.125 for cache read) and the 2026-11-11 Opus token-direction shares, computes the implied blended ratio, and asserts the README states both factors, a band that contains the blended ratio, and the same-day-lag / settled-day guidance. It fails on the current README. `make verify` passes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The ratio for 2026-11-12 is re-measured against the SETTLED Cost Explorer day, and the cause of any excess over the documented band is identified from the per-direction token counts.\n- [ ] Either the ceiling table is corrected or the README band is updated with the measured reason; no config key, env var or flag."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794524870644245813,"uuid":"965e96ca-22df-41cf-be96-4ff4a2ce6449"}